{"description":"Employer-authorized reads over the job-local Native Forms quiz module of Project To-dos. resource selects the read: forms (job library; jobId), form (one form with draft + published versions; formId), results (attempt summaries; jobId+formId), attempt (ONE attempt with submitted answers, grading rows, revision history, release state, and the sanitized expected-answer projection for auto-graded questions \u2014 never exposed to workers; attemptId), roster and export-csv (jobId+formId). attempt and export-csv accept delivery=resource: a compact receipt plus a resource_link (opentrain://project-todos/quizzes/attempts/{attemptId} or opentrain://jobs/{jobId}/project-todos/quizzes/forms/{formId}/results/csv{?formVersionId}) instead of the body. Worker emails are never included. Requires project_todos:read scope, a claimed account, and the default-off project-todos agent surface.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"attemptId":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"delivery":{"description":"Only for resource=attempt and resource=export-csv; any other resource refuses delivery. One attempt or one results export can pass the 25,000-token default MCP output limit. delivery=inline (default) returns the read in structuredContent, unchanged. delivery=resource returns a compact receipt (attempt: attemptId, formId, jobId, answerCount, expectedAnswerCount; export-csv: jobId, formId, formVersionId, filename, rowCount, redactions; both: resourceUri, contentType, byteSize, sha256) and a resource_link; the body never enters the result \u2014 read the linked resource when you need it. Both deliveries are bounded by the route's response, which the hosting platform caps at about 4.5 MB of JSON (HTTP 413 above it, on every surface). There is NO snapshot: a resource read re-fetches the LIVE read, so its _meta.sha256 equals the receipt hash only if nothing changed in b